{
  "name": "Driver COD Briefing",
  "description": "Daily 9pm Edmonton evening wrap-up: calls the RxDeliver driverCodBriefing function which pushes every driver who worked today a day summary (CODs collected today incl. cash, plus anything still outstanding), then the agent composes and sends the app owner a full briefing broken down by driver.",
  "trigger": {
    "condition": null,
    "config": {
      "trigger_type": "scheduled",
      "events": [],
      "schedule_mode": "recurring",
      "cron_expression": "0 21 * * *",
      "one_time_date": null,
      "timezone": "America/Edmonton",
      "interval_value": null,
      "interval_unit": null,
      "interval_anchor": null,
      "ends_type": "never",
      "ends_on_date": null,
      "ends_after_count": null
    }
  },
  "definition": {
    "document": {
      "dsl": "1.0.0",
      "name": "driver_cod_briefing",
      "namespace": "base44",
      "version": "1.1.0"
    },
    "do": [
      {
        "run_and_report": {
          "call": "invoke_superagent_step",
          "then": "end",
          "with": {
            "message": "It is 9pm — the evening driver COD wrap-up briefing is running now. Follow these steps exactly:\n\n1. Run this bash command (it triggers the RxDeliver briefing function, which sends push notifications to every driver who WORKED TODAY with their day's COD summary — collected today including cash, plus anything still outstanding — and returns the full grouped JSON):\ncurl -s -X POST 'https://base44.app/api/apps/68570f3cd01bfa2d2408a9d6/functions/driverCodBriefing' -H \"Authorization: Bearer $BASE44_SERVICE_TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'\n\n2. From the returned JSON, compose a compact app-owner briefing in PLAIN TEXT (WhatsApp, no markdown) broken down BY DRIVER (only the drivers listed in the JSON — those are the ones who worked today). For each driver show a header line like: ROBERT T — collected $ 36.44 (2) · outstanding $ 12.79 (1). Under it, list the collected items in the format: $ 36.44 · Cash · Melinda Martin, then the outstanding items in the format: $ 12.79 · 09/25(HS)-Marta Maingat.\nLAYOUT RULE: within each driver block, right-align the money column — pad all amounts (including the header totals) to the same width so every $ sign and decimal lines up vertically.\nEnd with the overall day totals (collected and outstanding) across drivers. Also note any driver whose push failed (pushes array shows sent/skipped/errors per driver) — mention delivery failures briefly at the end. If nobody worked today or there was no COD activity, just say so in one sentence.",
            "x-base44": {
              "description": "Evening COD wrap-up: push worked drivers, brief the owner",
              "title": "Driver COD evening wrap-up"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
